+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-patch-pointer-errors/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+## Context
+
+`pointerString` in `src/patch.ts` calls `parsePointer`, whose `JsonPointerError` propagates out of `applyPatch`. A review of the other operations against RFC 6902 found no other deviation.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Catch `JsonPointerError` in `pointerString` and rethrow `JsonPatchError` with the operation index and original message. Keeping `JsonPointerError` as the cause is unnecessary.
+- Other `parsePointer` calls in `applyPatch` receive already validated pointers, so they need no change.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Breaking for callers that matched `JsonPointerError` from `applyPatch`; the library is internal to the team and the new type is consistent with all other patch failures.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-patch-pointer-errors/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-patch-pointer-errors/proposal.md
