index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8364935e005f9d22bd3b072d32757b1f79d186f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-patch-pointer-errors/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+RFC 6902 treats an invalid patch and a failed operation alike: the whole patch is unsuccessful. `applyPatch` throws `JsonPatchError` for every failure except an invalid JSON Pointer in `path` or `from`, which surfaces as `JsonPointerError`. Callers catching `JsonPatchError` miss those failures.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `applyPatch` throws `JsonPatchError` when `path` or `from` is not a valid JSON Pointer string; the pointer error message is kept.
+- No change to successful behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+<!-- none -->
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: the patch validity requirement now specifies the error type for invalid pointers.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/patch.ts` and `src/patch.test.ts`. Callers that caught `JsonPointerError` from `applyPatch` must catch `JsonPatchError`.
